{"item_id": "syn-v1-01", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 75, "claim_support": 70, "edge_case_awareness": 80, "technical_accuracy": 85}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 70, "claim_support": 60, "edge_case_awareness": 75, "technical_accuracy": 90}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 73, "claim_support": 65, "edge_case_awareness": 78, "technical_accuracy": 88}}, "language": "en", "question_item": "q1", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_postgres_mvcc", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 6800, "segment_id": "seg_syn0101000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "Every update writes a new row version and keeps the old one until no snapshot needs it."}, {"end_ms": 26600, "segment_id": "seg_syn0102000000000AB", "start_ms": 7400, "text": "Each transaction reads a snapshot decided by xmin and xmax visibility rules, so readers never block writers. The cost is bloat from dead tuples, which VACUUM and autovacuum clean up; autovacuum also prevents transaction ID wraparound. For example, under repeatable read a long transaction keeps old versions alive."}], "session_key": "syn-en-1", "split": "dev", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-02", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 80, "claim_support": 80, "edge_case_awareness": 80, "technical_accuracy": 90}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 85, "claim_support": 75, "edge_case_awareness": 70, "technical_accuracy": 85}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 83, "claim_support": 78, "edge_case_awareness": 75, "technical_accuracy": 88}}, "language": "en", "question_item": "q2", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_idempotency", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 14800, "segment_id": "seg_syn0201000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "Clients send an idempotency key with every payment request. The server stores the key with a unique constraint in the same transaction as the payment record, so a retry returns the stored result instead of charging twice."}, {"end_ms": 37800, "segment_id": "seg_syn0202000000000AB", "start_ms": 15400, "text": "If a request with the same key is still in progress it gets a conflict, and keys expire after a day. Calls to the payment provider go through an outbox, and a reconciliation job compares our records with the provider's. For example, if the client times out and retries, the second request sees the first result."}], "session_key": "syn-en-1", "split": "dev", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-03", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 80, "claim_support": 75, "edge_case_awareness": 85, "technical_accuracy": 85}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 80, "claim_support": 70, "edge_case_awareness": 75, "technical_accuracy": 90}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 80, "claim_support": 73, "edge_case_awareness": 80, "technical_accuracy": 88}}, "language": "en", "question_item": "q3", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_latency_investigation", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 12000, "segment_id": "seg_syn0301000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "First I would scope it on the dashboard: which endpoints, which percentile, and when it started. Then I would check recent changes such as a deploy or a configuration change."}, {"end_ms": 27800, "segment_id": "seg_syn0302000000000AB", "start_ms": 12600, "text": "Tracing and a flame graph localize the slow part; tail latency often comes from lock contention, a cold cache, garbage collection or retries. To mitigate, roll back the release or scale out, and confirm each hypothesis before acting."}], "session_key": "syn-en-1", "split": "dev", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-04", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 5, "claim_support": 10, "edge_case_awareness": 0, "technical_accuracy": 10}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 10, "claim_support": 5, "edge_case_awareness": 5, "technical_accuracy": 15}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 8, "claim_support": 8, "edge_case_awareness": 3, "technical_accuracy": 13}}, "language": "en", "question_item": "q1", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_postgres_mvcc", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 7200, "segment_id": "seg_syn0401000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "I think PostgreSQL locks the row when you update it, so other readers wait until the transaction commits."}], "session_key": "syn-en-2", "split": "dev", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-05", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 10, "claim_support": 10, "edge_case_awareness": 5, "technical_accuracy": 30}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 15, "claim_support": 10, "edge_case_awareness": 0, "technical_accuracy": 25}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 13, "claim_support": 10, "edge_case_awareness": 3, "technical_accuracy": 28}}, "language": "en", "question_item": "q2", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_idempotency", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 6000, "segment_id": "seg_syn0501000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "I would just check in the database whether the payment already exists before inserting it."}], "session_key": "syn-en-2", "split": "dev", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-06", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 0, "edge_case_awareness": 10, "technical_accuracy": 10}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 0, "edge_case_awareness": 5, "technical_accuracy": 5}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 0, "edge_case_awareness": 8, "technical_accuracy": 8}}, "language": "en", "question_item": "q3", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_latency_investigation", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 4400, "segment_id": "seg_syn0601000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "I would restart the servers and see if it gets better."}], "session_key": "syn-en-2", "split": "dev", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-07", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 75, "claim_support": 70, "edge_case_awareness": 80, "technical_accuracy": 85}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 70, "claim_support": 65, "edge_case_awareness": 85, "technical_accuracy": 85}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 73, "claim_support": 68, "edge_case_awareness": 83, "technical_accuracy": 85}}, "language": "tr", "question_item": "q1", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_postgres_mvcc", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 6400, "segment_id": "seg_syn0701000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "Her güncelleme satırın yeni sürümünü yazar; eski sürüm, ona ihtiyaç duyan anlık görüntü kalmayana kadar durur."}, {"end_ms": 22200, "segment_id": "seg_syn0702000000000AB", "start_ms": 7000, "text": "Her işlem görünürlük kurallarıyla belirlenen bir anlık görüntü okur, bu yüzden okuyucular yazıcıları engellemez. Bedeli ölü satırların yarattığı şişmedir; VACUUM bunları temizler ve sarmalı (wraparound) önler. Örneğin repeatable read yalıtım düzeyinde uzun bir işlem eski sürümleri canlı tutar."}], "session_key": "syn-tr-1", "split": "test", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-08", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 85, "claim_support": 75, "edge_case_awareness": 80, "technical_accuracy": 90}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 80, "claim_support": 80, "edge_case_awareness": 85, "technical_accuracy": 80}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 83, "claim_support": 78, "edge_case_awareness": 83, "technical_accuracy": 85}}, "language": "tr", "question_item": "q2", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_idempotency", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 10000, "segment_id": "seg_syn0801000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "İstemci her ödeme isteğiyle bir idempotency anahtarı gönderir. Sunucu anahtarı ödeme kaydıyla aynı transaction içinde benzersiz bir kısıtla saklar; tekrar gelen istek kayıtlı sonucu alır."}, {"end_ms": 26600, "segment_id": "seg_syn0802000000000AB", "start_ms": 10600, "text": "Aynı anahtarla devam eden bir istek çakışma alır ve anahtarların süresi bir gün sonra dolar. Ödeme sağlayıcısına çağrılar bir outbox üzerinden gider ve bir mutabakat işi kayıtları karşılaştırır. Örneğin istemci zaman aşımına uğrayıp tekrar denerse ikinci istek ilk sonucu görür."}], "session_key": "syn-tr-1", "split": "test", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-09", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 80, "claim_support": 70, "edge_case_awareness": 80, "technical_accuracy": 85}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 75, "claim_support": 75, "edge_case_awareness": 85, "technical_accuracy": 80}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 78, "claim_support": 73, "edge_case_awareness": 83, "technical_accuracy": 83}}, "language": "tr", "question_item": "q3", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_latency_investigation", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 10400, "segment_id": "seg_syn0901000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "Önce metriklerde hangi uç noktaların ve hangi yüzdelik dilimin etkilendiğine ve sorunun ne zaman başladığına bakarım. Sonra son dağıtımı ya da bir yapılandırma değişikliğini kontrol ederim."}, {"end_ms": 24200, "segment_id": "seg_syn0902000000000AB", "start_ms": 11000, "text": "İzleme ve profil yavaş kısmı bulur; kuyruk gecikmesi çoğunlukla kilit çekişmesi, soğuk önbellek, çöp toplama ya da tekrar denemelerden gelir. Etkisini azaltmak için sürümü geri alırım ya da ölçeklerim ve her hipotezi doğrularım."}], "session_key": "syn-tr-1", "split": "test", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-10", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 0, "edge_case_awareness": 0, "technical_accuracy": 5}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 5, "edge_case_awareness": 0, "technical_accuracy": 10}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 3, "edge_case_awareness": 0, "technical_accuracy": 8}}, "language": "tr", "question_item": "q1", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_postgres_mvcc", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 2400, "segment_id": "seg_syn1001000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "Bilmiyorum, sanırım veritabanı güncellenen satırı kilitliyor."}], "session_key": "syn-tr-2", "split": "test", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-11", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 10, "claim_support": 5, "edge_case_awareness": 0, "technical_accuracy": 25}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 5, "claim_support": 10, "edge_case_awareness": 5, "technical_accuracy": 30}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 8, "claim_support": 8, "edge_case_awareness": 3, "technical_accuracy": 28}}, "language": "tr", "question_item": "q2", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_idempotency", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 3600, "segment_id": "seg_syn1101000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "Ödemeyi eklemeden önce veritabanında zaten var mı diye bakarım."}], "session_key": "syn-tr-2", "split": "test", "synthetic": true}
{"item_id": "syn-v1-12", "labels": {"adjudicated": null, "rater_a": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 0, "edge_case_awareness": 10, "technical_accuracy": 5}, "rater_b": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 0, "edge_case_awareness": 0, "technical_accuracy": 10}, "reference": {"architecture_maturity": 0, "claim_support": 0, "edge_case_awareness": 5, "technical_accuracy": 8}}, "language": "tr", "question_item": "q3", "rubric": {"rubric_id": "rub_demo_latency_investigation", "version": 1}, "segments": [{"end_ms": 2800, "segment_id": "seg_syn1201000000000AB", "start_ms": 0, "text": "Sunucuları yeniden başlatırım, düzelir mi diye bakarım."}], "session_key": "syn-tr-2", "split": "test", "synthetic": true}
